{"duration_api_ms":188688,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"138a0944-4ab9-424a-99be-30c965531420","total_cost_usd":0.24442000000000003,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15654,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":18180,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":12786},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15654,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":18180,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15654,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15654},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":18180,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":15654,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.24442000000000003,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":12786,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"The front is a one-parameter curve in flight-path angle at D≈3.384 m, bluntness 1.2, cone 70°. It runs from (227k W/m2, 417.9 K) at gamma -1.5 to (274.6k, 391.1 K) at gamma -3.57. Three limits pin it in place. Peak g reaches its 12 g cap at about gamma -3.57. Heatshield mass margin falls to about 0 at D≈3.385 m. Bluntness above 1.2 (and cone below about 69.6 at b=1.2) gives 'aero surface extrapolation' or invalid geometry, so the buildable region ends near b=1.2, cone 70. Little hypervolume is left, so I mostly fill small gaps in the gamma sweep at the largest allowed D (3.385) and add a few cheap probes of bluntness and cone in the valid region.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-92f6aed905e3 to C-636b6aeca4e0: at D=3.384, b=1.2, cone=70, flux rises 227k to 275k W/m2 while bondline T falls 417.9 to 391.1 K as gamma goes -1.5 to -3.57. The curve is convex and smooth.\",\"C-636b6aeca4e0 (max_g margin 8e-5) and C-112b974177e0 (max_g margin -6.5e-5 at gamma -3.572, D 3.38): gamma is capped near -3.57.\",\"C-81e40e27ff03 (D 3.385, mass margin 1.4e-4), C-636b6aeca4e0 (D 3.384, 7.4e-4) and C-112b974177e0 (D 3.38, 3.1e-3): mass-fraction margin drops about 0.6 per metre of D, so D is capped near 3.385 m.\",\"C-166a3a760ccb, C-3d41ce848a30, C-bcce2808c9b8, C-a554636d8035 (b 1.205 to 1.25) and C-2375647d7e43 (cone 69.0) all fail on surrogate extrapolation. C-ed967979f72a (b 1.3) fails on invalid geometry. Bluntness cannot rise above 1.2 at cone 70.\",\"C-ebb96199c3d5 (b 1.1, cone 68.5, D 3.35): flux 282k at gamma -3.5, higher than the b=1.2 curve (about 273k). C-d94e2f4145b9 (cone 69.6): flux and T lie on the same front.\",\"Designs at steeper gamma or small D (C-c76d29c9a126, C-02335773e828, C-2d91d8d713d7) are infeasible on max_g and have much higher flux, so they cannot improve the front.\"],\"mechanism\":\"This relies partly on prior Allen-Eggers-type reasoning, calibrated to the data. Peak g in a ballistic entry is set mainly by gamma, which caps gamma near -3.57. Flux falls with nose radius and area (roughly D^-1.4 here) and has a weaker dependence on bluntness. Bondline T falls with a shorter heat pulse at steeper gamma. The mass-fraction limit caps D near 3.385 m, and the surrogate's valid range caps bluntness at about 1.2 when cone is 70. The front is therefore one-dimensional in gamma, and proposals are interpolations at D=3.385 (which lowers flux and T by about 0.03% versus 3.384) plus small probes of cone and bluntness.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Interpolated values should be accurate to about 0.3%. The b=1.15 and b=1.1 probes carry hull-extrapolation and mass-margin risk (lower b appears to reduce mass margin). D=3.3851 sits within about 1e-4 of the mass-fraction limit, so rounding could make it infeasible. The dependence of g on D and geometry is estimated from very few points.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-92f6aed905e3\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -1.5 and -1.7 at the largest allowed D.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":229250,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":416.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Cheap fill-in near the shallow-gamma end of the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-6ca49a55e28f\",\"rationale\":\"Interpolate between gamma -1.85 and -2.2.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.95},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":236600,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":410.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a 0.35 deg gap in the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-6ca49a55e28f\",\"rationale\":\"Interpolate between gamma -1.85 and -2.2 (second point).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.05},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":238800,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":409.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the same gap with finer spacing.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-d6570e7303ea\",\"rationale\":\"Interpolate between gamma -2.2 and -2.5.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.35},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":245600,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":405.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a 0.3 deg gap in the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-f8e103c54279\",\"rationale\":\"Slightly shallower than gamma -2.5 at D=3.385.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":246770,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":404.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a gap; D=3.385 gives a marginally better point than the D=3.38 row C-ec735c51e3e5.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-f8e103c54279\",\"rationale\":\"Interpolate between gamma -2.5 and -2.7.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":251400,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":401.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a front gap at the largest allowed D.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-4dc37a3f4f3a\",\"rationale\":\"Interpolate between gamma -2.7 and -2.9.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.8},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":256150,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":399.35,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a front gap.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-9f046db94e96\",\"rationale\":\"Interpolate between gamma -2.9 and -3.05.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.98},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":260450,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":397.25,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a front gap.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-03553beb93b9\",\"rationale\":\"Interpolate between gamma -3.05 and -3.2.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.125},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":263950,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395.65,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a front gap.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-013d6de46fd0\",\"rationale\":\"Interpolate between gamma -3.2 and -3.3 at D=3.385.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.25},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":267000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Slightly better than the D=3.38 row C-1fe39bf5a810 at the same gamma.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e9fb95df2518\",\"rationale\":\"Interpolate between gamma -3.3 and -3.4.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.35},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":269400,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a front gap near the g cap.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-a201e4576c17\",\"rationale\":\"Interpolate between gamma -3.4 and -3.475.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.44},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":271550,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a front gap close to the g limit; predicted g about 11.78, so margin is comfortable.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-259ec4805a86\",\"rationale\":\"Interpolate between gamma -3.475 and -3.55.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.51},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":273200,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a front gap near the g cap.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-385f3798bd45\",\"rationale\":\"Between gamma -3.5 and -3.55 at D=3.385.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.53},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":273700,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a front gap near the g cap.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-385f3798bd45\",\"rationale\":\"Between gamma -3.55 and -3.57, just under the g cap.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.56},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274400,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Extends the front with a point close to the g limit.\",\"requested_fidelity\":1},{\"parent_id\":\"C-81e40e27ff03\",\"rationale\":\"Push to the g and mass corners: gamma just shallower than -3.57 and D slightly above 3.385. It should be feasible if the mass margin holds.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3851,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5695},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the exact corner; if the mass margin holds it marginally beats C-81e40e27ff03.\",\"requested_fidelity\":1},{\"parent_id\":\"C-d94e2f4145b9\",\"rationale\":\"Test cone 69.8, between valid 69.6 and 70, at gamma -3.5.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.8},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":273150,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.72,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks whether cone below 70 shifts the flux/T trade-off. C-d94e2f4145b9 suggests slightly lower flux and slightly higher T.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-259ec4805a86\",\"rationale\":\"Probe modest bluntness reduction (1.15) with D reduced to 3.38 to keep mass margin. It should stay inside the surrogate hull, since b<1.2 at cone 70 is bracketed by valid points.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.15,\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":276300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Measures the b sensitivity at cone 70. It is probably dominated but is informative about the hull edge and the mass dependence on b.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-92f6aed905e3\",\"rationale\":\"Shallowest gamma at D=3.385, a tiny improvement over C-92f6aed905e3.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":227270,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":417.85,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Marginally improves the low-flux end of the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-d6570e7303ea\",\"rationale\":\"Gamma -2.2 with D nudged to 3.3851.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3851},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":242100,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":407.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tiny improvement over C-d6570e7303ea; checks the mass margin at D=3.3851.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ebb96199c3d5\",\"rationale\":\"Isolate the cone effect at b=1.1: cone 70 and D 3.375 (D reduced to keep mass margin, since lower b reduces margin).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.375,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":279300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether a b<1.2 design near cone 70 offers any different trade-off, and probes the surrogate hull around b=1.1.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":147337,"type":"result","duration_ms":188729,"uuid":"e8c8dd35-37c8-48ce-8e74-61430a4d0f99","ttft_stream_ms":1277,"time_to_request_ms":39,"first_content_frame_ms":1277,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
